DGGAL

rs4dggs-ogc depends on the rs4dggs library, which is a Rust port of the algorithms of DGGAL,
the Discrete Global Grid Abstraction Library, whose copyright holder is Ecere Corporation. The
notice below, which the library carries, applies to this crate through it.

rs4dggs is a Rust port of the algorithms of DGGAL.

The port reproduces DGGAL's numeric constants verbatim. At the sites its own source and
documentation cite, it also reproduces the operation order that DGGAL v0.0.6, as built by
its own compiler settings, performs where that order departs from the order its eC source
text spells.

It is a modified work: in a few places it departs from DGGAL's answers on purpose (among
them the aperture-3 sub-zone orders corrected at some rhombus-edge zones, four kinds of
entry left out of the aperture-7 neighbour lists, and every zone's vertices given
anticlockwise), each described under "Departures from the engine" in its README.

rs4dggs and rs4dggs-ogc contain no DGGAL source code and no DGGAL binary. DGGAL serves only
as the oracle of their test suites, which run a separately installed copy; it is not
distributed with these crates.

